<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>DSCR Loans in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Investor mortgage options</p><h1>DSCR Loans in Miami</h1><p>Rental property loan options for Miami investors using property cash flow instead of traditional personal income documentation.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Review My Rental Scenario</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Request Investor Quote</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>DSCR loans are commonly used by real estate investors who want financing based on the rental property’s income potential rather than traditional employment income. The debt service coverage ratio compares rental income to the proposed payment.</p><p>In Miami, DSCR loans may be used for condos, single-family rentals, townhomes, and certain investment properties, depending on property type and program guidelines.</p><h2>How DSCR loans are evaluated</h2><p>Lenders may review market rent, lease income, appraisal rent schedule, taxes, insurance, association dues, occupancy, borrower credit, reserves, and property condition.</p><p>The stronger the property cash flow and borrower profile, the more options may be available.</p><h2>Miami investor considerations</h2><p>Investors should review short-term rental rules, HOA restrictions, condo eligibility, insurance cost, flood exposure, local rent assumptions, and reserves before relying on a projected return.</p><p>The mortgage quote should be compared with realistic taxes, insurance, HOA fees, maintenance, vacancy, and management costs.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a DSCR Loans Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>DSCR Loans in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Do DSCR loans require personal income verification?</summary><p>Many DSCR programs focus on property cash flow instead of traditional personal income, but documentation requirements vary by lender.</p></details><details><summary>Can DSCR loans be used for Miami condos?</summary><p>Sometimes. The condo project, rental rules, and lender guidelines all need to be reviewed.</p></details><details><summary>Are DSCR loans only for experienced investors?</summary><p>Some programs may allow newer investors, while others prefer experience. The exact requirements depend on the lender and scenario.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="investment-property-loans-miami.html">Investment Property Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="bank-statement-loans-miami.html">Bank Statement Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="condo-loans-miami.html">Condo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Mortgage Calculator Florida<span>→</span></a></div></div></section></main>
